          "default": "output/pretraining_checkpoints/run-1/checkpoint-1"
        },
        "mode": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "decay",
          "enum": [
            "continue",
            "decay"
          ],
          "description": "FOOTGUN: the stock default mode is \"decay\". Flipping only is_resume: true starts a decay run, not a continuation. Always set mode explicitly. Two resume modes: continue - finish the original token/step budget from the checkpoint with the original schedule. Takes NO decay_* fields. decay - anneal a stable-end trunk checkpoint over an additional budget. Set exactly one of decay_tokens / decay_steps. decay_shape is OPTIONAL (falls back to schedule default). lr_decay_to_fraction is REQUIRED for mode: decay. NOTE: decay restarts the dataloader from the start of a pass, so a resume-decay matches a single-run wsd decay bit-for-bit only when the trunk's stable->decay boundary is data-pass aligned; keep global_batch_tokens / world_size identical to the trunk's run. continue | decay"
        },
        "decay_tokens": {
